  "estimators": "Precision and recall of the dedup rule on the labeled pairs, weighted back to all pairs.\n\nPairs were drawn through units with a known per-draw probability p (pairs.py). Within a stratum\nthe Hansen-Hurwitz estimate of a pair total is mean(z / p) over the drawn pairs, so a pair through\na unit with few partners counts for few pairs and one through a template hub for many. Totals add\nover strata; precision and recall are ratios of totals. Pairs labeled unsure are left out, and the\nstratum mean is taken over the pairs that remain (assumes unsure is unrelated to the label).\n\nIntervals: percentile bootstrap that resamples pairs within each stratum, so every stratum keeps\nits size. A stratum with no positive pair contributes zero positives in every resample, and the\nbootstrap cannot say how many it misses; `missed_upper` gives the rule-of-three bound for that.\n",
  "notes": [
    "unsure pairs are excluded from every estimate",
    "id links between trudvsem API and snapshots are taken as the same vacancy and are not in the sample",
    "rule.* scores the pairwise decision; entity.* scores membership in one connected component",
    "rule.* held-out scores are clean: the rule was fixed on the tuning half before the held-out half was scored",
    "entity.* held-out scores are optimistic: the component constraints (one INN, one settlement, one street; place kept for remote sole proprietors) were added after the held-out pairwise errors had been seen, and the sole-proprietor case removes held-out pair d0004 directly",
    "recall over all pairs is not estimable from this sample: four strata hold no positive pair, and recall_worst_case is the rule-of-three bound if they held 3/n of their pairs"
  ]
